  "findings": "The adopted chart fixes 60 EC per year and the exact 12 EC thesis despite the specialisation subtable. The catalogue confirms 120 EC with QRM II, all first-year courses and at most two unfinished second-year units at application. The group paper develops research design and peer criticism. The UCR policy route has economic methods with direct welfare, taxation and bank-risk work; the qualitative and marketing route applies the shared methods to consumer evidence. The banking course materially covers pricing and risk, and the accounting course includes project appraisal. The target Finance specialisation continues with dedicated corporate finance and investments. The closest UCR route already uses the strongest finance contributions, and a further route does not establish a distinct concentration. The applied econometrics overlap is real but the UCR course does not establish VU’s dedicated Probit, time-series and panel extensions. All 48 placements and prerequisite checks pass. The options differ by 52.5 EC each way. All 25 external components and 31 selected UCR courses resolve, and the optional research remains separate.",
  "result": "passed"
